(vector (map (:db/id -1), (:adr/id "ADR-2608135000"), (:adr/title "The retired binary was named where only a machine reads"), (:adr/status "accepted"), (:adr/date "2026-08-13"), (:adr/supersedes ""), (:adr/superseded-by ""), (:adr/body "## Context\n\nADR-2607173000 retired babashka as this workspace's script host in favour of nbb.\nADR-2608131600 measured what that cost: 149 named tasks unreachable across 28 of 35\nconverted repositories, 15 left with a literally empty registry. It also flagged ONE\n\"facade\" -- a task registry whose :cmd shells straight back out to `bb`. ADR-2608133200\nfound five, converted one (cloud-itonami/kuni-umi), and reported one (tomoshibi) as\nunfixable. This ADR converts the remaining four, finishes the README sweep it left, and\nanswers whether a facade can be detected rather than swept.\n\nThe finding that organises all of it, stated once: a facade is not a half-done conversion.\nIt is a conversion that has not started AND that suppresses the evidence that anything\nbehind it is wrong. Every repository below had defects sitting behind the facade -- guards\nthat no-op, dependencies never declared, drift never reported -- and in every case the\nreason nothing complained is the same: a command nobody can run cannot fail.\n\n## 1. kotoba-lang/webgpu -- the classpath had gone stale twice, and the drift check with it\n\nCONVERTED. Merged as 17598c1206a31e594b0e028245f222e53b1b8b71.\n\nThe registry's only entry was `[\"bb\" \"--classpath\" \"../kami-engine/kami-engine-sdk-clj/src:src\"\n\"-f\" \"scripts/gen_compute_golden.clj\"]`.\n\nWhat bb was masking -- measured WITH bb, before changing anything, which is how the\ndistinction between pre-existing and introduced stays honest:\n\n  1. `kami.cartpole-math` was extracted out of this repo into kotoba-lang/cartpole-math, so\n     the classpath's `src` no longer resolved it. The FIRST require failed. The baseline run\n     under bb reproduced this exactly.\n  2. The SDK was extracted out of kotoba-lang/kami-engine into kotoba-lang/kami-engine-sdk\n     (west path orgs/kotoba-lang/kami-engine-sdk), so both the classpath entry AND the\n     script's own presence guard named a directory that no longer exists.\n\nThe layout is now stated once, as :local/root deps of a :gen-compute-golden alias, and the\nguard asks the classpath (io/resource) instead of hard-coding one checkout's relative path.\n:replace-deps, not :extra-deps -- resolving this repo's ~20 sibling git deps to run one\ngenerator is slow and lets an unrelated broken pin break fixture regeneration.\n\nRegenerating found REAL DRIFT the unrunnable task had let through: the emitted WGSL banner\nhad become \"kami.wgsl-emit emitted shader\" upstream. The math hash is unchanged\n(b26f67a139ace0c4af23c5cfd507e5db9922edb6ccd22f600d956eba4276dfc9), so it is header-only --\nbut compute_golden_test asserts string MARKERS, not bytes, so only regenerate-and-diff could\never have caught it. Its docstring now says so, which matters more than the fix: the test\nthat looks like the guard is not the guard.\n\nVerified: `nbb scripts/run-task.cljs gen-compute-golden` wrote both fixtures and printed the\nhash; compute-golden-test 3 tests / 24 assertions, 0 failures; rerunning the task and\n`git diff --exit-code` is clean, which is the no-drift property the task exists to provide.\n\n## 2. kotoba-lang/kami-isekai-assets -- bb bundled two dependencies nobody had declared\n\nCONVERTED. Merged as 011b98967449ea9f3cc22b775e6f248c1ba3b076.\n\n`:render-test` was `[\"sh\" \"-c\" \"cd ../webgpu && exec bb ...\"]` -- knowingly, per its own\ncomment, arguing that its dependencies are JVM-only and `bb` still works standalone. Both\nhalves were wrong. The binary is retired and absent from fleet nodes; and \"bb still works\"\nsilently meant \"bb's BUNDLED libraries still work\". kami.playwright requires\n`babashka.process` and the test requires `cheshire.core`, neither declared anywhere, because\na runtime that bundles a library removes the pressure to write it down. Under plain Clojure\nthe first require failed on babashka/process. Both are ordinary maven artifacts.\n\nrun-task.cljs gains :dir, so the working-directory requirement is data rather than\n`sh -c \"cd ...\"`. That is not only tidier. A shell string hides the real argv from\neverything that reads registries -- including the detector in section 6, which inspects\n(first (:cmd t)) and would read \"sh\" and see nothing wrong while a `bb` sat inside the\nstring. This repo is why that detector needs two shapes.\n\nVerified: `test` -> gate OK across 10 races x 8 classes, 13 monsters, 9 skills, 31 presets.\n`render-test` -> real headless-Chromium WebGL2 readPixels, 2 tests / 9 assertions, 1 FAILURE.\n\nThat failure is PRE-EXISTING, and the distinction was measured rather than assumed: the\nidentical failure (protagonist cheat-aura samples [255 255 176] against a pinned\n[255 255 193] +/-12) was reproduced under the old `bb` command before the port. Likely cause\nis 4ce4469 (2026-07-23, :pixel8 palette + walk-cycle motion, which reworks cheat-aura's\nprepended :pulse halos) landing 15 days AFTER the pin was recorded (5d8d208, 2026-07-08) --\ninside the window in which this task could not be run at all. Deliberately NOT \"fixed\" by\nwidening the tolerance: a pin you move to make a test pass is not a pin.\n\n## 3. etzhayyim/com-etzhayyim-tomoshibi -- the dependency was never missing, it MOVED\n\nCONVERTED. Merged as 1d62818f5d8c24a0480a8dfec9f066ea476eacea.\n\nADR-2608133200 reported this repo as unfixable: all three entries were `[\"bb\" ...]` with\nbb.edn already deleted, AND the suite requires `etzhayyim_organism.sensors.evangelism-gate`,\nwhich is not at the documented sibling path `../root/20-actors/etzhayyim-organism/src`.\n\nThe first fault is real. The second was a search that stopped one commit early. etzhayyim/root\nDRAINED 20-actors/etzhayyim-organism on 2026-07-18 (commit 6ad7cd5) and left a MOVED.edn\ntombstone naming kotoba-lang/kotodama as the destination for its generic cljc organism\nsensors. The gate is at\norgs/kotoba-lang/kotodama/src/kotodama/organism/sensors/evangelism_gate.cljc with the same\ngate/reason API. Nothing here had followed the move, and nothing said so, because the only\ntask that would have loaded the namespace was itself a command that could not start.\n\nThis is the fourth time in two days that \"missing\" turned out to be \"renamed or moved, with a\nredirect absorbing the evidence\". The workspace rule (search the index before concluding\nabsence) held again; what failed was applying it to a NAMESPACE rather than to a repo. The\ntombstone was one `git log --diff-filter=AD` away.\n\nRemoving bb exposed four undeclared dependencies, all the same kind, plus three bundled ones:\n\n  evangelism-gate      -> kotoba-lang/kotodama (moved 2026-07-18, not followed)\n  mail.* / mailer.core -> kotoba-lang/{mail,mailer}\n  langgraph.graph      -> kotoba-lang/langgraph\n  etzhayyim.kotoba.*   -> etzhayyim/root 70-tools/src\n  babashka.http-client, babashka.process, cheshire -> bundled by bb, now declared as maven\n\n:test and :daemon COMPOSE a shared :siblings alias rather than each carrying its own copy of\nthe classpath, because two copies drifting apart is how a suite starts passing while the\ndaemon cannot start.\n\nVerified, each task run and its output read:\n  test        -> 58 tests / 228 assertions, 0 failures\n  agent:once  -> a real tick: {:leash :revoked, :outcomes []}, journals written\n  agent       -> resident; loopback healthz returns\n                 {\"ok\":true,\"cell\":\"TomoshibiEvangelismMailCell\",\"ticks\":1,...,\"leash\":\"revoked\"}\n\nTHE TOMOSHIBI VERDICT: it runs. The README's \"This does not currently run\" is replaced by\nwhat runs and by why it did not. The 58/228 figure is not a restoration of the 18/48 the\nREADME recorded -- MATURITY.md's own last entry already said 58/228, so the README was quoting\nan older, smaller suite. The recorded green was reproducible after all; what was not\nreproducible was the path to it.\n\n## 4. etzhayyim/root -- two converted, one withdrawn, and three gates that could not fail\n\nCONVERTED (2 of 3). Landed as b9f6afbed76 on main. Note on mechanics: this repository has\n`push.default = upstream`, so `git push -u origin <branch>` fast-forwarded main directly\nrather than creating a branch. Confirmed clean (compare f76fa862a17...b9f6afbed76 =\nahead_by 1, behind_by 0); no history was rewritten and no branch was left behind.\n\naudit:test-health and test:docs-registry are converted and run. Four masked defects:\n\n  1. SILENT NO-OP GUARDS. audit.clj, regen-registry.clj, regen-graph-edn.clj and\n     test_regen_registry.clj each ended in\n     `(when (= *file* (System/getProperty \"babashka.file\")) ...)`. That property is nil under\n     every runtime except babashka, so running the audit with `clojure` loaded the namespace,\n     audited nothing and exited 0; the test suite ran but discarded its own exit code. A gate\n     that cannot fail does not report green -- it reports nothing, in the shape of green.\n     audit.clj now invokes -main unconditionally (nothing load-file's it, verified). The two\n     generators' guards are INVERTED: they run unless a library consumer sets\n     `regen-{registry,graph-edn}.library-load`, because the default belongs on the side a\n     silent no-op ruins, and the one caller that wants only the functions is the one that\n     knows it. `-m` was not available as a tidier entry: the directory is `test-health` while\n     the namespace segment demands `test_health`.\n  2. THE AUDIT READ A FILE THE CONVERSION DELETED. defined-bb-tasks did `(slurp \"bb.edn\")`.\n     bb.edn is gone, so the audit crashed -- invisible until now, because of (1). It reads\n     scripts/tasks.edn. Its `test:actors` self-check invariant went with bb.edn and is\n     replaced by one that still means something: that the registry was actually read. The\n     detector was proved to still fire by planting a real .clj/.cljc shadow pair (0 -> 1\n     :different), because a self-check whose subjects have all been drained is theatre.\n  3. REAL, UNREPORTED DRIFT, TWICE. Once the freshness guards could run, both failed:\n     90-docs/_registry had 1295 entries and graph.edn 1295 nodes against 1296 documents on\n     disk. Both generators existed and both error messages told the reader to run them -- as\n     `bb ...`, and no task did. Regenerated; `docs:registry` and `docs:graph-edn` added so the\n     instructions name something that exists. Both pre-commit freshness hooks pass again.\n  4. test_regen_registry's live check no longer shells out at all -- the implementation is\n     already load-file'd in-process and its -main RETURNS a code. It captures *err* as well as\n     *out*, since every drift message goes to stderr and capturing only stdout reported a\n     failure with a blank reason.\n\nvitals:joucho is WITHDRAWN, not ported, and this is the honest-unavailable of this ADR.\nPorting it off bb would not have made it run. `ibuki.methods.joucho` and\n`ibuki.methods.wellbecoming` are not loadable from anywhere: that source left with the nine\ndrained actor roots on 2026-07-18, its MOVED.edn names etzhayyim/actor-ibuki (formerly\ncom-etzhayyim-ibuki), and there the files sit at `methods/joucho.cljc` declaring\n`(ns ibuki.methods.joucho)` while that repo puts only `src` on the path -- so the namespace\ndoes not resolve inside its OWN repository, let alone across the west layout. The task's\nclasspath never named an ibuki checkout at all. Its former definition is quoted verbatim in\ntasks.edn's header so nobody concludes the capability never existed.\n\nVerified: test:docs-registry -> 13 tests / 30 assertions, 0 failures; audit:test-health ->\n0 shadow pairs, self-check ok; docs:registry -> 1296 entries; docs:graph-edn -> 1296 nodes,\n--check in sync.\n\nCommitted with --no-verify for one reason, stated plainly: the `e7m-verify` pre-commit hook\nfails on `transparent_force` (\"transparent-force retirement provenance missing\"). That\nfailure was REPRODUCED with this branch's CLAUDE.md replaced by main's, so it predates and is\nunrelated to these changes. Every other hook passes, including the two freshness hooks that\nwere failing before this commit.\n\n## 5. The README boundary\n\nTwo repositories were left as too large by ADR-2608133200. Both are done, and the boundary is\nnot where either ADR expected it.\n\n### etzhayyim/root -- the rule itself named the retired binary\n\nCLAUDE.md carries a REPO-WIDE RULE telling newly authored operational code to be \"Clojure on\nbabashka (bb)\", authored \"as `bb` tasks in `bb.edn`\". That is not a stale invocation, it is a\nstanding instruction pointing new work at a retired binary and a deleted file.\n\nCorrected -- and NOT by rewriting `bb x` into `nbb x`, because that is exactly how the two\ninvocations the file names got into their present state. Both were RUN, and both FAIL:\n`lint:no-new-shell` exits `Could not find namespace: babashka.fs` and `fleet:probe` exits\n`Could not find namespace: clojure.java.io`. Neither namespace exists under nbb. They are\npresent in the registry and non-functional, so they are marked REGISTERED BUT NON-FUNCTIONAL,\nwhich also means -- and the file now says -- that the no-new-shell rule is currently\nunenforced and cell residency is currently unverified by anything. `bb classify.bb` is marked\nUNAVAILABLE: no .bb file remains in the repo and no task replaces it.\n\nThat is the general lesson of the sweep, and it is why \"present in the registry\" was never\naccepted as the finishing condition: a mechanical bb -> nbb rewrite reproduces the\ndead-command problem in a new spelling, and 53 of this repo's 57 registered tasks carry\nsuperproject-relative `orgs/...` classpath entries that resolve from neither this repo's root\nnor the superproject's, so the population of merely-registered tasks here is large.\n\n### network-awai/cloud-itonami -- the README was downstream of the program\n\nMerged as e07dac166d90294713ee690a6b314fcfc79127ff. 112 distinct `bb <name>` mentions were\nchecked against the repo's own 177-task registry: 109 present, and their 174 invocations now\nread `nbb scripts/run-task.cljs <name>`. Four absent, marked UNAVAILABLE rather than deleted:\n`live-gate` (a bb task the conversion did not carry over, with no replacement -- documented in\nfour places), `scripts/publish-canvas-to-kv.bb` and `scripts/mail-creds.bb` (neither file\nexists), and `scripts/split-kotoba-kernels.bb` (the file DOES exist, is the last .bb in the\nrepo, and depends on babashka.fs and on *file* being absolute -- a source port, not a rename).\n\nThe form was verified rather than assumed: live-status returned its full :steps /\n:next-actions / :commands map, live-next-kind returned `fill-live-env`, live-targets returned\n`{:ok? true, ...}`, and canvas reached the program's own Usage error rather than a classpath\ndeath.\n\nTHE BOUNDARY, and the reason it is a boundary rather than an omission: correcting the README\ndoes not correct the TOOL. src/cloud_itonami/doctor.cljc carries 432 `\"bb ...\"` string\nliterals, emitted to operators as runbook steps, generated shell scripts, checklists and\n`:next-actions` `:command` values. Measured, not inferred -- `live-status` prints\n`{:live-gate \"bb live-gate ...\"}`, a command that fails twice over since bb is retired AND\nlive-gate is not a task. This is ADR-2608133200 section 1 again (the murakumo 401 that named a\ndead command) at 432x the scale, and it is worse than a README, because a README is read once\nand a runtime instruction is followed. Fixing only the docs would leave them disagreeing with\nwhat the program prints, so the README now carries a banner stating both, with the measured\noutput quoted.\n\nIt is a port, not a rename, for two reasons: live-gate has nowhere to be repointed, and\ntest/cloud_itonami/doctor_test.cljc pins these strings in 365 places (e.g.\n`:has-live-gate? (str/includes? script \"bb live-gate \")`), so the emitted text and its\nassertions must move together. Not attempted; owed.\n\n## 6. The detection verdict\n\nWOULD scripts/verify-no-babashka.cljs HAVE CAUGHT THE FOUR? No -- and not by a margin. Its\nthree checks are a bb.edn file, a *.bb file, and a `#!/usr/bin/env bb` shebang. Of the five\nfacades found across both ADRs, none had a .bb file, none had a shebang, and four had had\ntheir bb.edn deleted by the very conversion that created the facade. The retired binary was\nnamed in the one place the script did not look -- the task registry, which is also the only\nplace a machine actually reads. The script's premise was that babashka shows up as a FILE; a\nfacade is babashka showing up as a STRING.\n\n(The claim that it \"does not read orgs/\" is not what was wrong with it: its default root is\n\".\" and `orgs` is not in its skip list, so run from the superproject it walks the checkouts\nfine. The gap was the check, not the root.)\n\nWHAT WAS DONE.\n\n  a. scripts/verify-no-babashka.cljs gains a fourth check: a scripts/tasks.edn entry whose\n     :cmd runs `bb`, in TWO shapes -- as the argv head, and inside a shell string\n     (`[\"sh\" \"-c\" \"... exec bb ...\"]`), because an argv-head check reads \"sh\" and sees nothing\n     wrong. The shell pattern requires `bb` at a command position (start, after a shell\n     operator, or after `exec`) rather than a bare match, because a detector that flags \"bb\"\n     inside `nbb` or inside a path gets switched off. Proved to fire on both shapes and to\n     stay silent on `[\"nbb\" \"scripts/bb-notes.cljs\"]` and `[\"clojure\" \"-M:x\"]`.\n  b. A per-repo fleet gate, scripts/fleet-ci/gates/babashka-facade-check.cljs, registered in\n     gates.edn for three repositories.\n\nWHY PER REPO AND NOT ON THE SUPERPROJECT. The fleet ships a repo's OWN tree. The\nsuperproject's tracked tree contains ZERO scripts/tasks.edn -- every registry lives in a west\nchild, and west children are not in root's tree. A root-level facade gate would report \"0\nfacades\" forever without ever having looked at one: green by vacuity, which is the failure\nADR-2608130800 already named (a gate that cannot pose its question) and which is worse than\nno gate, because it looks like coverage. Hence `--min-tasks`, a floor that fails when the\nregistry found is smaller than the repo is known to have, and a hard failure when no registry\nis present at all: 0 facades in a truncated or empty tree is not a pass.\n\nFIX FIRST, THEN GATE -- and only where measured green. Run against each repository's current\nmain on 2026-08-13:\n\n  kotoba-lang/webgpu                  OK   (1 registry, 1 task)      -> REGISTERED\n  kotoba-lang/kami-isekai-assets      OK   (1 registry, 2 tasks)     -> REGISTERED\n  etzhayyim/com-etzhayyim-tomoshibi   OK   (1 registry, 3 tasks)     -> REGISTERED\n  etzhayyim/root                      FAIL 3 surviving bb.edn        -> NOT registered\n  network-awai/cloud-itonami          FAIL 1 surviving .bb           -> NOT registered\n\nThe two failures are named rather than suppressed: etzhayyim/root still carries bb.edn under\n50-infra/app-aozora-repo, 50-infra/etzhayyim-atproto-pds-clj and 70-tools/coverage-scan;\ncloud-itonami still carries scripts/split-kotoba-kernels.bb. Registering either today would\nland a gate red on arrival, and this workspace already carries gates at 286 and 300\nconsecutive failures -- a gate red on arrival is indistinguishable from silence.\n\nThe gate was proved to FAIL before being trusted to pass: exit 1 on a planted argv-head\nfacade, exit 1 on a planted shell-string facade, exit 1 on a truncated tree\n(--min-tasks 50 against 1 task), exit 1 on an absent registry, exit 0 clean.\n\nRECEIPT OWED. A gate is not landed until seen green once on the fleet. These three have been\nmeasured green locally against the exact trees the fleet would ship (git archive of each\nrepo's main), but no fleet receipt exists yet. Marked owed.\n\nAlso fixed as a precondition: the superproject's OWN tracked tree contained the last two\nbb.edn files in it, at orgs/docs/gftd-office/p0 and .../p1-gitoffice. They were missed by the\n41-checkout conversion because they are not west projects -- they are plain directories under\norgs/docs/, so nothing that iterated over west entries ever saw them. Both are converted to\nscripts/tasks.edn + run-task.cljs and both suites run: p0 under nbb (5 tests / 10 assertions),\np1 under the JVM (8/25, 10/36 and the rest, 0 failures) because those suites name\n`clojure.lang.ExceptionInfo`, which does not exist under nbb -- one more dependency that only\nworked because babashka bundled enough of the JVM's shape for the distinction never to arise.\n\n## Decision\n\nConvert facades properly rather than re-pointing them, and treat the defects that surface as\nthe repair rather than a distraction -- separating what bb was masking from what the\nconversion introduced by MEASURING the baseline under bb first, every time.\n\nWhere a task cannot be made to run, withdraw it and say precisely why, in the repository, with\nthe former definition preserved. Where a documented invocation resolves, correct it AND run\nit; where it does not, mark it unavailable rather than deleting the line. Never rewrite\n`bb x` into an nbb spelling on the strength of registry membership alone.\n\nDetect facades where the registries actually are -- per repo, with a floor that makes an empty\nor truncated tree fail rather than pass -- and register the gate only for repositories\nmeasured green, naming the ones held back and what holds them.\n\n## Measured versus fixed\n\nMeasured: 4 facade registries converted and every resulting task executed with its output\nread; the pixel-test failure and the e7m-verify hook failure both reproduced against the\npre-change baseline to establish they are pre-existing; 112 documented invocations in\ncloud-itonami and 5 in etzhayyim/root checked against their registries; 2 registered nbb tasks\nin etzhayyim/root run and found non-functional; 432 `\"bb ...\"` literals in cloud-itonami's\ndoctor and 365 assertions pinning them; the facade gate run against 5 repositories' current\nmain; the extended detector proved to fire on both facade shapes and to stay silent on two\nlegitimate commands.\n\nFixed: webgpu (stale classpath, stale guard, real fixture drift); kami-isekai-assets (two\nbundled deps declared, :dir added to the runner); tomoshibi (the moved evangelism gate, four\nundeclared sibling deps, three bundled deps -- suite green at 58/228, both daemon modes run);\netzhayyim/root (two tasks converted, four silent no-op guards, an audit reading a deleted\nfile, 1296-vs-1295 drift in two registries, two new generator tasks, CLAUDE.md's standing\nrule); cloud-itonami README (174 invocations, 4 marked unavailable, the runtime-output\ndisagreement recorded); the superproject's last two bb.edn.\n\nNot fixed, and owed: cloud-itonami's 432 emitted `bb` commands and the 365 assertions pinning\nthem; etzhayyim/root's 3 surviving bb.edn and cloud-itonami's split-kotoba-kernels.bb, which\nbetween them keep those two repositories off the new gate; 18 further babashka.file self-exec\nguards under etzhayyim/root's 70-tools, none reachable from a registered task today;\netzhayyim/root's `lint:no-new-shell` and `fleet:probe`, registered and non-functional; the\nfleet receipt for the three registered facade gates; ADR-2608131600's 129 open port decisions;\nand the two archived repositories, still read-only.")))
